# ArcDroid authored ROM/ADF; A3000, neutral input, 24 fresh then 24 reset frames.
# Characterization of the current retro_reset path (D-137 / QA L6).
# Early reset frames differ from a fresh load: programmed VIDC registers persist
# across machine recreation (initvid/vidc_reset). Pre-existing Arculator behaviour;
# Fable carries the register-reset change as a separate follow-up, outside R1.
# Video: harness FNV-1a over every XRGB8888 pixel byte in row order, without pitch
# padding; offset 1469598103934665603, multiplier 1099511628211, modulo 2^64.
# CI Linux x64 and Windows x64 (also local macOS arm64) are little-endian, so the
# full pixel-byte order is identical. Duplicate presentation retains that hash.
# PCM: FNV-1a offset 14695981039346656037 over every offered stereo int16 sample,
# explicitly low byte then high byte; pair count is every offered stereo pair.
# Geometry: frontend-announced width x height after each retro_run.
# No platform-dependent field is included; no pixel, PCM, count, geometry or
# startup frame is excluded. Text comparison normalizes only LF/CRLF newlines.
arculator-reset fresh frame=0 video=f3ee4d06bf3e0383 pcm=0e86a0ab215b02d5 pairs=983 geometry=640x480
